  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 214 PM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nThe cold front that swept across the area yesterday continues to mix \nnorthward as a warm front. Some lingering stratus remains while the \nshower activity has lifted north of the area by late morning. Due to \nlimited mixing from morning stratus, a wide range of temperatures \nare anticipated today with the cooler or more seasonable air \nremaining draped across parts of central and northern KS while \nsummer-like conditions prevail across much of southeast and portions \nof south central KS. An isolated late day or early evening \nshower/storm may be possible as the cap weakens but activity is\nexpected to be limited due to increasing subsidence from the \nmid/upper ridge which is slowly building back into the region. \nThere is some concern that low clouds/patchy fog could redevelop\nover parts of central KS as they remain within a weak easterly\nupslope regime with narrow dewpoint depressions progged \ntonight.\n\nThe mid/upper ridge over the Tennessee Valley is progged to \nretrograde into the Mississippi Valley area/Southern Plains by late \nin the week allowing summer-like heat and dry conditions to remain \ndraped across the area Thu-early Sat. As we move into the weekend, a \nrobust shortwave trough is progged to move into the Central and \nNorthern Rockies. This will help break down the ridge on Saturday \nwhile driving a cold front southward into the Central Plains on \nSunday. The prefrontal trough may become a focus for deep moist \nconvection on Saturday afternoon while the front arrives late \nSaturday night into Sunday providing an additional focus for showers \nand thunderstorms. Much cooler and more seasonable air is expected \nto arrive across the area on Sunday and persist as we head into the \nupcoming week. Average highs for Sept 19-20 are in the lower 80s and \naverage lows are in the upper 50s. More seasonable air is \nanticipated in the wake of the front on Sunday while lingering into \nthe middle of next week. A stable post-frontal regime is anticipated \nearly next week but some low pops were maintained at this time given \nthe forecast uncertainty.",
